cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this replication, please cite the original paper (below), not this file."
title: "Replication: Artificial Intelligence, Algorithmic Pricing, and Collusion"
abstract: >-
  Independent replication of Calvano, Calzolari, Denicolo and Pastorello (2020,
  AER 110(10): 3267-3297). Re-implements the Q-learning pricing environment,
  the convergence and equilibrium-play diagnostics, the deviation/punishment
  analysis and the strategy graphs, and resolves an internal calibration
  inconsistency in the paper's printed demand function (kappa = 1/mu).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Coursework replication (AI-assisted)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/calvano-2020-algorithmic-pricing-collusion-replication"
url: "https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.20190623"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - algorithmic collusion
  - algorithmic pricing
  - reinforcement learning
  - Q-learning
  - Bertrand competition
  - logit demand
  - computational economics
  - replication
